# Copy to .env.local and fill in from Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys.
# .env.local is gitignored. Never commit real values.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# The browser key. New projects issue a publishable key; older ones have a
# legacy JWT anon key. Either name works — set whichever your project shows.
# Both are safe in a browser bundle: row-level security is what protects the
# data, and they grant no more than the signed-in user already has.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# The secret / service_role key is deliberately NOT listed here.
#
# It bypasses row-level security completely: every table, every row, no
# permission checks. It belongs only in a server-side secret store, never in
# a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, never in a file under version control, and never
# pasted into a chat. Nothing in this app needs it, and lib/env.ts refuses to
# start if one is supplied.
